{"nodes": [{"id": "claude_keepqueue_client", "label": "keepqueue-client Sub-Project", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "Project Overview", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Next.js App Router frontend with React 19 and TypeScript. CLAUDE.md states Next.js 15 while the client README states Next.js 16 \u2014 the two docs disagree on the major version."}, {"id": "claude_keepqueue_server", "label": "keepqueue-server Sub-Project", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "Project Overview", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Express REST API in TypeScript on the Firebase Admin SDK, kept as a separate deployable from the client so privileged Firestore writes never run in the browser."}, {"id": "claude_in_memory_cache_architecture", "label": "Server In-Memory Cache Architecture", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "Architecture > Server: In-Memory Cache", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "All Firestore collections are loaded into a singleton cache at startup so there are zero per-request database queries; /data/* endpoints filter and transform the in-memory copy and /actions/* endpoints write Firestore then update the cache. Trades memory footprint and single-instance correctness for read latency and Firestore read cost."}, {"id": "claude_client_server_authentication", "label": "Firebase ID Token Bearer Authentication", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "Architecture > Client to Server Communication", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Every client request attaches a Firebase ID token as Authorization: Bearer, so the Express API delegates identity entirely to Firebase Auth and keeps no session store of its own."}, {"id": "claude_direct_firestore_reads", "label": "Direct Client Firestore Reads", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "Architecture > Client to Server Communication", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The client bypasses the Express API and reads Firestore directly for real-time data, giving live subscriptions the REST API cannot provide; the cost is a second data path whose consistency with the server cache is not enforced anywhere."}, {"id": "claude_server_route_structure", "label": "Server Route Structure (/actions and /data)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "Architecture > Server Route Structure", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Routes are split by effect rather than by resource: /data/* is read-only against the cache and /actions/* mutates Firestore and refreshes the cache. All handlers use the RouterService signature and forward errors via next(error); bodies are Zod-validated before handlers run and responses go through jsonOK/jsonFailed."}, {"id": "claude_zustand_persisted_stores", "label": "Zustand Persisted Client Stores", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "Architecture > Client: Zustand State", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Three persisted stores (auth, businesses, settings) all wrapped by a createSelectors utility so components subscribe granularly (useAuthStore.user()) instead of selecting from the whole store, avoiding re-renders on unrelated state changes."}, {"id": "claude_app_router_layout", "label": "Next.js App Router Layout", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "Architecture > Client: App Router Layout", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Routes segment by audience \u2014 /auth, /business/*, /customer/*, /home/[businessId] for the public booking flow, /landing-page. Convention is to minimize 'use client' and prefer React Server Components, with dynamic imports for heavy components, to keep the client bundle small."}, {"id": "claude_internationalization", "label": "Hebrew/English Internationalization and RTL", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "Architecture > Internationalization", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "JSON translation files for en and he behind a useLanguage() hook exposing t(key), isRtl and lang; Hebrew flips the whole layout to dir=\"rtl\" and moves the sidebar to the right, so direction is a first-class layout input, not a styling afterthought."}, {"id": "claude_shared_types_manual_sync", "label": "Manually Synced Shared Types", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "Architecture > Shared Types", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Client and server each keep their own src/types/global.ts with the same definitions (User, Business, Service, CalendarEvent, WaitItem, NotificationLog, MessageTemplate) and must be kept in sync by hand \u2014 no shared package, so drift is possible and is a known risk. NotificationType is narrowed to sms|email after WhatsApp was removed."}, {"id": "claude_ui_conventions", "label": "UI and Code Conventions", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "Key Conventions", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Functional components only, Tailwind + shadcn/ui + Radix UI with no inline styles, custom utilities .center/.col/.full/.ellipsis, and project-wide disabling of no-explicit-any, no-unused-vars and exhaustive-deps ESLint rules \u2014 velocity favored over strict lint enforcement."}, {"id": "keepqueue_client_lib_helpers_api_apicall", "label": "apiCall", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "keepqueue-client/lib/helpers/api.ts", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "keepqueue_client_lib_helpers_api_serverurl", "label": "serverUrl", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "keepqueue-client/lib/helpers/api.ts", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Environment switch baked into a module constant: localhost:9000 in dev, the Render-hosted production URL otherwise, so no build-time env var is required for the API base."}, {"id": "keepqueue_server_src_managers_cachemanager_cachemanager", "label": "CacheManager", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "keepqueue-server/src/managers/cacheManager.ts", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Singleton exposing typed get/set/delete/merge over the whole Firestore mirror; being a singleton is what makes the no-per-request-query design work and also what makes it unsafe to scale to multiple server instances without an invalidation channel."}, {"id": "keepqueue_server_src_firebase_initialcache_initsnapshot", "label": "initSnapshot", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "keepqueue-server/src/firebase/initialCache.ts", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Bootstraps the in-memory cache from Firestore at server startup; every /data endpoint depends on this having completed."}, {"id": "keepqueue_client_lib_store_utils_createselectors", "label": "createSelectors", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "keepqueue-client/lib/store/utils.ts", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "keepqueue_client_lib_store_authstore_useauthstore", "label": "useAuthStore", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "keepqueue-client/lib/store/authStore.ts", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "keepqueue_client_lib_store_businesses_usebusinessesstore", "label": "useBusinessesStore", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "keepqueue-client/lib/store/businesses.ts", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "keepqueue_client_lib_store_settingsstore_usesettingsstore", "label": "useSettingsStore", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "keepqueue-client/lib/store/settingsStore.ts", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "keepqueue_client_hooks_index_uselanguage", "label": "useLanguage", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "keepqueue-client/hooks/index.ts", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "keepqueue_server_src_middlewares_index_validatebody", "label": "validateBody", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "keepqueue-server/src/middlewares/index.ts", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "keepqueue_server_src_helpers_index_jsonok", "label": "jsonOK", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "keepqueue-server/src/helpers/index.ts", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "keepqueue_server_src_helpers_index_jsonfailed", "label": "jsonFailed", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "keepqueue-server/src/helpers/index.ts", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "keepqueue_server_src_types_index_routerservice", "label": "RouterService", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "keepqueue-server/src/types/index.ts", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "One handler signature (req, res, next) => void enforced across every route so error propagation is uniform via next(error) instead of per-route try/catch."}], "edges": [{"source": "claude_keepqueue_client", "target": "prd_keepqueue", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.95, "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "Project Overview", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "claude_keepqueue_server", "target": "prd_keepqueue", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.95, "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "Project Overview", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "claude_keepqueue_client", "target": "keepqueue_client_readme_keepqueue_client", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "Project Overview", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "claude_keepqueue_server", "target": "keepqueue_server_readme_keepqueue_server", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "Project Overview", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "claude_in_memory_cache_architecture", "target": "keepqueue_server_src_managers_cachemanager_cachemanager", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "Architecture > Server: In-Memory Cache", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "claude_in_memory_cache_architecture", "target": "keepqueue_server_src_firebase_initialcache_initsnapshot", "relation": "references", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.95, "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "Architecture > Server: In-Memory Cache", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "keepqueue_server_src_firebase_initialcache_initsnapshot", "target": "keepqueue_server_src_managers_cachemanager_cachemanager